ALTERED-SOURCE DISCLOSURE (required by Zlib clause 2)
  The Zlib license requires that "Altered source versions must be plainly marked as such, and must
  not be misrepresented as being the original software." Cathode carries a local modification to
  Blend2D and marks it here.

  Patch      : Cathode/patches/blend2d-assign-data-underalloc.patch
  Applies to : blend2d/core/array.cpp, function bl_array_assign_data
  Change     : one line — the new impl is sized from `n` (the new element count) instead of `u.size`
               (the array's previous size). Upstream sizes the buffer from u.size but then writes
               n * item_size bytes, which overflows the allocation whenever n exceeds the current
               capacity (for example, any assign into a freshly constructed array).
  Status of the change upstream: present on upstream master at the pinned commit above; not fixed
               upstream as of 2026-06. This is a Cathode-local alteration, not an upstream revision.

  IMPORTANT — CURRENT APPLICATION STATE. As of this writing the patch is NOT applied by any build
  step in this repository. It is carried as source only. Wiring its application into the vendor
  build is deferred work (tracked as the vendor/build item in sprint 033's deferral roadmap).
  Consequently a Blend2D built from this repository today is UNALTERED upstream code at the pin
  above, and carries the upstream defect described. This disclosure is stated in the forward-looking
  sense required by clause 2 — it plainly marks the alteration Cathode distributes in source form —
  and deliberately does not imply the patched build is live.

